{"title":"Clinical Researcher Roadmap","role":"Clinical Researcher","summary":"A Clinical Researcher designs, coordinates, conducts, analyzes, or supports research involving human participants, healthcare interventions, clinical outcomes, medicines, medical products, and healthcare practices.","facts":{"Current degree":"BHMS (Homoeopathy)","Course":"Homoeopathic Medicine & Surgery"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Clinical Researcher designs, coordinates, conducts, analyzes, or supports research involving human participants, healthcare interventions, clinical outcomes, medicines, medical products, and healthcare practices."},{"type":"p","text":"For a BHMS graduate, this pathway combines the clinical understanding gained through Homoeopathic Medicine and Surgery with clinical research methodology, biostatistics, research ethics, clinical-trial operations, scientific writing, data management, and evidence evaluation."},{"type":"h","text":"Potential work environments include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical research organizations (CROs)"},{"type":"h","text":"Research hospitals"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic institutions"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical research units"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare research organizations"},{"type":"h","text":"Public-health organizations"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical and healthcare companies"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical-device organizations"},{"type":"h","text":"Regulatory and pharmacovigilance teams"},{"type":"h","text":"Homoeopathy research institutions"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A BHMS degree provides a healthcare/clinical foundation, but it does not by itself make someone qualified to independently design, approve, or lead every type of clinical study. Clinical research roles have different requirements depending on the position, study type, institution, ethics requirements and applicable